Deloitte Consulting LLP seeks a Senior Consultant in Dallas, Texas.
Work You’ll Do
Drive innovative and transformative solutions for clients that address their next generational needs. Create effective visions, strategies and roadmaps, in direct alignment and support of business and technology objectives for clients within Retail and Consumer Products sector. Develop future-state business process and key design decisions for critical strategic and operational areas. Conduct market analysis, including determining current and future competitive environments of business entities. Conduct technical enablement assessment to determine key process and organizational gap in current trade promotion management activities. Analyze industries to synthesize quantitative and qualitative financial market information, key players, and industry trends. Analyze financial and budgeting processes to identify cost levers for reduction and optimization. Assist clients in developing a shared services organization and improving back-office efficiencies by eliminating duplication and streamlining processes with a focus on stakeholder management via feasibility studies, global best practices and standards, industry benchmarks, and process scopes.
- 50% Travel required nationally
- Telecommuting permitted

Requirements
Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, any STEM field, or a related field and 2 years of related work experience in the job offered or in a related occupation.
Position requires 2 years of related work experience in each of the following:
- Developing enterprise, customer, and operating model strategies and advising clients on how to grow their business and achieve target cost structures, utilizing Salesforce Sales Cloud, Salesforce Configure, Price, Quote (CPQ), Salesforce Revenue Cloud, and Salesforce Revenue Cloud Advanced (RCA);
- Developing and documenting internal business services processes and metrics in a manner consistent with Six Sigma and Lean methodologies, utilizing Lucidchart and Salesforce Flow;
- Providing industry insight and analytical support using data mining, pattern matching, data visualization, and predictive modelling to produce analysis and algorithms utilizing Salesforce Reports and Dashboards;
- Utilizing Salesforce Flows, Triggers, and Salesforce CPQ to provide scalable designs and technical solutions to clients;
- Capturing business requirements, creating high-level design documents, and implementing analytical solutions using Jira, Confluence, Salesforce Business Analyst, and Agile methodology;
- Working across all phases of the Agile and Waterfall methodologies and Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) for product and strategy insight solutions for enterprise-level clients;
- Designing and implementing enhancements, process improvements, and custom solutions that are flexible and resilient to changing operational strategy using Salesforce CPQ, Salesforce Flow Builder, and Salesforce Process Builder; and
- Designing and developing reports and dashboards to measure performance metrics of clients, utilizing Salesforce Reports and Dashboards and Tableau CRM.

Deloitte Consulting LLP seeks a Senior Consultant in Minneapolis, Minnesota.
Work You’ll Do
Drive software advisory and implementation services to help companies unlock the value of technology investments as discrete services or comprehensive solutions. Perform assessments of existing information systems and identify gaps between business requirements and current system capabilities; provide application analysis to meet software architecture and infrastructure goals. Define systems strategy, develop system requirements, design, prototype, and test custom technology solutions, and support system implementation. Participate in setting engagement objectives and scope, develop work plans for components of engagements, and coordinate activities between workstreams and identify changes in scope. Provide industry insight and analytical support using data mining, pattern matching, data visualization, and predictive modeling tools to produce analysis and algorithms that help businesses make better decisions. Transform detailed requirements into a complete, detailed systems design document; support creation of interface specifications and call flows for the various components in the design.

• 50% Travel required nationally
• Telecommuting permitted
Requirements
Bachelor’s degree or foreign equivalent in Business Administration, any STEM field, or a related field and 2 years of related work experience in the job offered or in a related occupation.
Position requires 2 years of experience in the following:
- Utilizing Anaplan, Agile Delivery Methodology, Financial Planning and Analysis Maturity Model, Driver-Based Planning (DBP), and Integrated Business Planning (IBP) to provide software advisory and implementation services for clients in Technology, Media and Telecommunications (TMT) and Consumer industries;
- Researching user reported issues with software systems, identifying root causes and resolutions, and implementing fixes, utilizing Anaplan Model History, Selective Access Analysis, Dimensional Consistency Checks, List Hierarchy Validation, Formula Dependency Tracing, data import error logs, and Regression Comparison;
- Tracking implementation defects, coordinating defect resolution efforts, and documenting resolution details, utilizing Agile Defect Tracking, Jira, Severity Classification, and Root Cause Documentation (RCA);
- Creating project charters, schedules, and plans, defining project tasks, allocating resources, and monitoring project progress utilizing Agile and Hybrid methodologies, Smartsheets, Sprint Plans, Risks, Actions, Issues, and Dependencies (RAID) logs, and Milestone Tracking Dashboards;
- Working across all phases of the Agile lifecycle to design, develop, test and implement Annual Operating Plan (AOP), Rolling Forecast, Long-Range Planning (LRP), Workforce Planning, Capital Planning, and Management Reporting Dashboards for enterprise-level clients;
- Interfacing directly with client stakeholders to gather, analyze, and translate functional and technical requirements into project designs to deliver solutions that fully meet client needs, utilizing structured stakeholder interviews, Requirements Traceability Matrix (RTM), user stories, acceptance criteria documentation, backlog grooming, and sprint review workshops;
- Utilizing Anaplan Testing Approach, Anaplan model copy environments, Excel-based test scripts, test case repositories, defect logs, UAT sign-off trackers, and controlled data validation checklists to ensure successful design and implementation of solutions; and
- Analyzing and documenting current-state systems, processes and environments to support project design of future-state/to-be systems, processes and environments, utilizing Business Process Modeling (BPM), Financial Planning and Analysis Operating Model Assessments, DBP, integrated planning design principles, and Anaplan Solution Architecture Standards.

Other
Annual Salary: $119,000.00 - $198,400.00

Deloitte Consulting LLP seeks a Senior Consultant in Tempe, Arizona.
